@yesitzmeh Ummm ... no, it doesn't.

To "disseminate" means to spread, scatter, disperse or distribute.  Like the wind moves pollen, birds spread chili seeds, or furry mammals transport cheatgrass, tackweed and cockleburs.

The government, and its opposition, disseminate opposing propaganda.  The health administration disseminates proper hygiene information and disease statistics.  Newspapers and news websites disseminate the news.

